{"id": "rijks-20025806", "status": "ok", "meta": "A procession in the Dominican church in Antwerp, with a wall of paintings by Rubens and others, painted by Peeter Neeffs in 1636.", "about": "A procession moves through the nave of the Dominican church in Antwerp, now Saint Paul's church. Churchgoers and visitors stand at the left and right. A row of large paintings hangs on the left wall, with works by Rubens, Van Balen, Teniers, Jordaens and Caravaggio. Peeter Neeffs the Elder dated it 1636 on the first column at the left.", "museum_record": "https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/nl/collectie/object/SK-A-288--726b246f95fceeb2c845f889ddb4b733", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/nl/collectie/object/SK-A-288--726b246f95fceeb2c845f889ddb4b733", "https://id.rijksmuseum.nl/20025806"], "check": "clean"}
