{"id": "wd-Q19923605", "status": "ok", "meta": "Four figures eat a round ricotta in Vincenzo Campi's The Ricotta Eaters, about 1585, with the painter as Pantalone.", "about": "The Ricotta Eaters is an oil on canvas painting of about 1585 by Vincenzo Campi, showing four figures eating a round ricotta. He called it Buffonaria, tying its figures to Commedia dell'arte characters, and painted himself as Pantalone in red. Wikipedia says the ricotta on the tray seems to form a skull, a memento mori. Jacques Bernard gave the work to the Museum of Fine Arts in Lyon in 1875.", "museum_record": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Ricotta_eaters-Vincenzo_Campi-MBA_Lyon_H673-IMG_0324.jpg", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Ricotta_eaters-Vincenzo_Campi-MBA_Lyon_H673-IMG_0324.jpg", "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q19923605", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ricotta_Eaters"], "check": "clean"}
