{"id": "cma-86108", "status": "ok", "meta": "A Chinese servant walks in the rain, attributed to the monk-painter Gakuō Zōkyū with a spurious seal of Tenshō Shūbun, 1500s.", "about": "The painting is attributed to Gakuō and carries a spurious seal of the Shōkokuji temple monk-painter Tenshō Shūbun, who died around 1444 to 1450 and with whom Gakuō is said to have trained. Gakuō may have come from Ise, south of Kyoto. Not much is known about his life, but inscriptions on some of his paintings show strong ties to eminent monks in Kyoto's major Zen temples.", "museum_record": "https://clevelandart.org/art/2015.512", "inventory_number": "2015.512", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "Gift from the Collection of George Gund III", "sources": ["https://clevelandart.org/art/2015.512", "https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/86108"], "check": "clean"}
