{"id": "si-chndm_2007-27-85", "status": "ok", "meta": "Queen Victoria's private sitting room at Buckingham Palace, with slipcovered furniture and a draped piano, by James Roberts, about 1840.", "about": "This interior is identified as Queen Victoria's private sitting room. A semicircular alcove is at the right and a fireplace at the left, and French windows shaded by striped awnings lead to a balcony. Slipcovered furniture gives a sense of intimacy, most of all an English tête-à-tête seen from behind, and a draped piano stands at lower right. Portrait paintings in elaborate gilt frames hang on the facing wall and the left wall. James Roberts made the picture around 1840.", "museum_record": "https://collection.cooperhewitt.org/view/objects/asitem/id/230049", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://collection.cooperhewitt.org/view/objects/asitem/id/230049"], "check": "clean"}
