{"id": "si-fsg_F1911.209", "status": "ok", "meta": "The shore of West Lake in the Southern Song capital Lin'an, with pleasure boats that Marco Polo described, painted by Li Song.", "about": "This painting shows the shore of the famous West Lake in Lin'an, the Southern Song capital, now Hangzhou, which Marco Polo visited. He wrote that the lake was provided with a great number of boats, big and small, for pleasure trips, roofed over with decks on which men stood and pushed poles into the lake bottom to move the barges where they were told. The painting is attributed to Li Song.", "museum_record": "https://asia.si.edu/object/F1911.209/", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://asia.si.edu/object/F1911.209/"], "check": "clean"}
