{"id": "si-npg_NPG.76.37", "status": "ok", "meta": "Lillian D. Wald, founder of the Nurse's Settlement House, painted by William Valentine Schevill in 1910.", "about": "Lillian Wald grew up in a well-off German-Jewish community in Cincinnati and was expected to live a life of ease. A chance meeting with a nurse opened what she called a window on a new world. While teaching home nursing to immigrants in lower Manhattan, she visited a student's home and saw the poverty and filth of the tenements firsthand. In 1895 she founded the Nurse's Settlement House and a visiting nurse service. William Valentine Schevill painted her portrait.", "museum_record": "https://npg.si.edu/object/npg_NPG.76.37", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://npg.si.edu/object/npg_NPG.76.37"], "check": "clean"}
